import{_ as r,o as i,c as t,a3 as o}from"./chunks/framework.1Y430-yj.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Practical Exercise: A Coupled Xircon–Yazhen Syringe Line Using 120 Ferrium Ore","description":"","frontmatter":{"lang":"en-US","translationSource":{"title":"实战演练 120蓝铁的壤晶-蓝药耦合产线解析","archivedAt":"2026-10-23T14:20:34.857Z","url":"https://docs.qq.com/aio/DTmluZ1diWlpQZldw?p=LYKER2bG6lsxJFNfTATAAO","scope":"page"}},"headers":[],"relativePath":"logistics/src/page-LYKER2bG6lsxJFNfTATAAO.md","filePath":"logistics/src/page-LYKER2bG6lsxJFNfTATAAO.md","lastUpdated":null}'),n={name:"logistics/src/page-LYKER2bG6lsxJFNfTATAAO.md"};function a(s,e,l,c,u,d){return i(),t("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<div class="logistics-content"><span class="logistics-source-anchor" id="实战演练-120蓝铁的壤晶-蓝药耦合产线解析" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="logistics-source-anchor" id="practical-exercise-a-coupled-xircon–yazhen-syringe-line-using-120-ferrium" aria-hidden="true"></span><h1 id="practical-exercise-a-coupled-xircon–yazhen-syringe-line-using-120-ferrium-ore" tabindex="-1">Practical Exercise: A Coupled Xircon–Yazhen Syringe Line Using 120 Ferrium Ore <a class="header-anchor" href="#practical-exercise-a-coupled-xircon–yazhen-syringe-line-using-120-ferrium-ore" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Practical Exercise: A Coupled Xircon–Yazhen Syringe Line Using 120 Ferrium Ore&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Source page ID: <code>LYKER2bG6lsxJFNfTATAAO</code> ｜ <a href="https://docs.qq.com/aio/DTmluZ1diWlpQZldw?p=LYKER2bG6lsxJFNfTATAAO" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open in Tencent Docs</a></p></blockquote><p>This example analyzes control chains in a complex production line.</p><p><span id="source-block-HhISoB2bc087pBeT853rjG"></span></p><span class="logistics-source-anchor" id="参考视频" aria-hidden="true"></span><h3 id="reference-video" tabindex="-1">Reference Video <a class="header-anchor" href="#reference-video" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Reference Video&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Endfield/AIC: Full-Rate-Port Balancing without Empty Storage—Marker Stone: 210 Xiranite + 150 Cuprium + 120 Ferrium Ore + 55 Dense Powder = Heavy Xiranite, Hetonite, Syringes, SC Batteries, Xircon. Jump directly to 05:04.</p><p><a href="https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV11eYi6hEwt/?share_source=copy_web&amp;vd_source=3b974227efd90987cb6375fbe49d61b8&amp;t=304" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Endfield/AIC: Full-Rate-Port Balancing without Empty Storage—Marker Stone, 210 Xiranite+150 Cuprium+120 Ferrium Ore+55 Dense Powder=Heavy Xiranite, Hetonite, Syringes, SC Batteries, Xircon</a></p><blockquote><p>This is basically my 1.5 build. I will stop designing whole-map lines and tinker with broad-range Cuprium/Xiranite adaptation instead.</p></blockquote><p>The Xircon line comes from 高级干员君 @樊二のいすぼくろ赛高. It is not fully adaptive yet: less powder reduces Xiranite use; more powder blocks powder. Without the Purification Node, this propagates to the Heavy Xiranite side of the Cuprium/Xiranite module.<br> @bear-冰梦潇湘 made a version merging Yinglung Pass and Marker Stone entirely into the main base, but placement is difficult: no pipe components outside the main base, and Inergen/acid must be routed across regions. If truly needed, message him or me.</p><p>For Yinglung Pass, BV1RdtU6TECG: copy the version releasing Xiragen, or modify it so the acid-mixing machine&#39;s 24 Xiranite directly powers four solidification machines; this prevents blocking.<br> For Jingyu Valley, copy Strongest AIC BV1tgbW6RE6W or @Xersyo&#39;s 1.4 design; they are similar.</p><p>Another reason not to copy: after placing this, you will immediately need to switch to Chubby Lung. Might as well put Xircon at the main base. (</p><p><span id="source-block-egkOJpa0bNQsJwYtsPDwhe"></span></p><span class="logistics-source-anchor" id="蓝铁路线" aria-hidden="true"></span><h3 id="ferrium-route" tabindex="-1">Ferrium Route <a class="header-anchor" href="#ferrium-route" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Ferrium Route&quot;">​</a></h3><p>We have 120 Ferrium Ore: 73.75 for Xircon, the remaining 46.25 for Yazhen Syringe [C].</p><p>Space prevents homogenizing Ferrium then splitting it equally for syringes, or building a large exact-ratio splitter. We therefore apply blocking-based production layer by layer, controlling flows to meet requirements. Ferrium allocation (a <u>split-like</u> line) should follow <strong>external conditions → controlled-branch flow → free-branch flow</strong>. This requires <u>the designed controlled branch to actually block, and the designed free branch to remain flowing</u>.</p><p>First subtract the 60 Ferrium Ore allocated to the powder for 60 Xircon. Another 13.75 Xircon remains. We want enough Ferrium for Xircon, with the remainder for syringes: <strong>Xircon output → Ferrium Powder supply → Ferrium supply for syringes</strong>. Powder supply must therefore be controlled. After refining 30 Ferrium Ore, <u>less than half suffices</u>, so use <strong>halving</strong>. Below, the red route from Shredding Unit to crucible blocks throughout: controlled, theoretical 15-, actual 13.75. Green directly carries Ferrium downward: free, theoretical 15+, actual 16.25.</p><p><img src="/endfield-logistics-wiki/logistics/src/assets/images/img-36519de571967588.q90-7f4251b745260574.webp" alt="Coupled Xircon–Yazhen Syringe Line Using 120 Ferrium Ore"></p><p>The lower route also feeds a Refining Unit at full 30 Ferrium Ore, all for syringes, but needs <strong>allocation between Fitting and Moulding Units</strong>. The terminal Packaging Unit synchronizes their flows, so <u>either branch can be controlled and still work</u>. Simply take two output belts from the Refining Unit, <u>equivalent to halving</u>. Since 16.25 Ferrium already enters the Moulding Unit from above and each machine actually needs only 23, the upward half to Moulding (red) blocks: controlled, theoretical 15-. The Fitting route (green) is free, theoretical 15+. Control: <strong>controlled Ferrium flow → free Ferrium flow</strong>.</p><p><img src="/endfield-logistics-wiki/logistics/src/assets/images/img-18545614db82d447.q90-075e993e35c748ad.webp" alt="Coupled Xircon–Yazhen Syringe Line Using 120 Ferrium Ore"></p><p>Simply merging at the Moulding Unit consumes about 11.5 Ferrium from each route. But the upper free branch carries 16, so it cannot flow freely. It must enter first, with the lower controlled branch supplying the remainder. Control: <strong>upper free Ferrium flow → lower controlled Ferrium flow</strong>.</p><p><img src="/endfield-logistics-wiki/logistics/src/assets/images/img-64eb5d65efd93ba6.q90-841c805d34e49d39.webp" alt="Coupled Xircon–Yazhen Syringe Line Using 120 Ferrium Ore"></p><p>At the Packaging Unit, its <u>merge-like</u> character means the blocked Moulding–Filling route is instead controlled by the flowing Fitting route: <strong>free Ferrium flow entering Packaging → controlled Ferrium flow entering Packaging</strong>.</p><p><img src="/endfield-logistics-wiki/logistics/src/assets/images/img-001c59b8eea7dfb9.q90-7d023b8eacd56293.webp" alt="Coupled Xircon–Yazhen Syringe Line Using 120 Ferrium Ore"></p><p>Overall: Xircon rate → Ferrium Powder production (upper controlled) → upper Ferrium to Moulding (upper free) → lower Ferrium to Moulding (lower controlled) → lower Ferrium to Packaging (lower free). Lower Ferrium to Moulding also depends on Packaging rate, which, due to its merge-like behavior, depends on the lower free branch. Thus lower free also controls lower controlled, forming a control loop whose input is upper Ferrium to Moulding.</p><blockquote><p>Understand the lower Ferrium–Packaging–Moulding system as a functioning module that accepts external Ferrium and turns it into more syringes.</p></blockquote><p><span id="source-block-jp73ArbRdnOznVCYZ5MKnI"></span></p><span class="logistics-source-anchor" id="产线中其余的阻塞情形" aria-hidden="true"></span><h3 id="other-blocking-in-the-line" tabindex="-1">Other Blocking in the Line <a class="header-anchor" href="#other-blocking-in-the-line" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Other Blocking in the Line&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The Xircon line needs 34.65 Sewage. The upper 30 has higher priority and can all enter the conduit. Lower-conduit Sewage should fill the remaining demand without accumulating, with excess disposed of. Only 4.65 remains, so after halving, red is controlled at 15-, green free at 15+, as planned. Actual demand automatically balances them to 4.65 and 25.35.</p><p>Without upper-Sewage priority, its flow is constrained by the free branch from the Converger perspective (red), blocking upper Sewage.</p><p><img src="/endfield-logistics-wiki/logistics/src/assets/images/img-4924a8449930c807.q90-29f919f22534b3c5.webp" alt="Coupled Xircon–Yazhen Syringe Line Using 120 Ferrium Ore"></p><p>The Converger at the small crucible&#39;s outlet lowers that outlet&#39;s priority. The output pipe needs 32.9 Xircon Effluent; the other branch supplies 2.5 plus the Purification Node&#39;s 12. With sufficient Liquid Xiranite, the crucible supplies up to 30, so the outlet must block. Ordinary merging of crucible output with 2.5+12 would also work: 14.5 is less than half 32.9, so the crucible blocks down to consuming 18.4 Liquid Xiranite. Placing the Converger directly at the outlet is simply more reliable.</p><p><img src="/endfield-logistics-wiki/logistics/src/assets/images/img-b4f4ff9659245655.q90-3a273e9e8deab707.webp" alt="Coupled Xircon–Yazhen Syringe Line Using 120 Ferrium Ore"></p><p><a href="./page-o3yxqfGNALKamNYPO1eu1t">2.5 Is a Stash Not Just a Special Splitter? (Core Content ⭐)</a></p><p><a href="./page-2kENbD6F4B8qcMtdPdudqt">2.6 Empty Storage? Full Storage? We Need More Oversupply!</a></p><blockquote><p>Translation note: The source rounds 16.25 to 16 and describes the machines’ requirement as 23; those figures are retained. “Dense Powder” refers contextually to Dense Originium Powder.</p></blockquote></div>',1)])])}const h=r(n,[["render",a]]);export{g as __pageData,h as default};
